      "entity": "Harold King",
      "scope": "political career",
      "claim": "Harold King is known for representing the South Australian House of Assembly seat of Chaffey for the Liberal and Country League from 1956 to 1962.",
      "answer": "representing the South Australian House of Assembly seat of Chaffey for the Liberal and Country League from 1956 to 1962",
      "quote": "Harold King (politician) Harold Welbourn King (11 July 1906 – 24 August 1983) was an Australian politician who represented the South Australian House of Assembly seat of Chaffey for the Liberal and Country League from 1956 to 1962. King had been a bank official, packing shed executive and fruitgrower before entering politics. He was elected to the Legislative Assembly at the 1956 election, defeating 18-year independent incumbent and government critic William MacGillivray after the LCL exchanged preferences with Labor to oust MacGillivray.",
      "original_document_number": 4
